{"study_accession":"PRJNA642175","secondary_study_accession":"SRP268939","title":"Chromatin accessibility and gene expression maps of Plasma Cells and Myeloma Plasma Cells [RNA-seq]","description":"We report the application of paired Assay for Transposase-Accessible Chromatin (ATAC-seq) and RNA-seq data to profile the regulatory landscape and expression of 5 primary Plasma Cell (PC), 28 Multiple Myeloma (MM) PC as well as 5 cell lines samples. Findings discriminated MM and MM subgroup-specific changes such as the exclusive overexpression of CCND1 and CCND2 oncogenes. DNA accessibility changes were correlated to gene expression in a topologically constrained manner to elucidate novel enhancer - promoter interactions, genes and pathways critical for myeloma biology and developmentally activated or de novo formed enhancers. Additionally, the MM subgroup-specific TF network dependencies were studied to help identify prognostic markers. Finally, we discover and functionally validate the critical enhancer that regulates ectopic expression of CCND2 in MM. Overall design: Examination of paired ATAC-seq and RNA-seq data of 5 primary Plasma Cell (PC), 28 Multiple Myeloma (MM) PC as well as 5 cell lines samples.","pubmed":"34521827","geo_series":"","n_samples":33,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN15378693","study_accession":"PRJNA642175","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"RNA-seq_A28.15","description":"RNA-seq_A28.15","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4643290","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-07-04","attributes":[["source_name","Primary plasma cell multiple myeloma"],["tissue","Bone marrow"],["condition","MM"],["cytogenetics","t(11;14) - CCND1"],["primary subgroup","CCND1"],["selected surface markers","CD138+"],["sequencing batch","3"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR12099715","experiment_accession":"SRX8624384","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":38091517,"base_cou